bin/

# Build output: docs/docs/build-* gets populated by per-PR doc-build
# preview runs (not on main). Without this rule, `git add -A` in any
# worktree that has run `pnpm install` or `pnpm build` will sweep
# them up (this exact trap bit a hygiene commit on this branch).
#
# NOT ignoring `docs/content/*.md` here even though my worktree had
# untracked ones — main has 12 *tracked* `docs/content/*.md` files
# (`ai.md`, `cache.md`, `contributing.md`, etc. — Docusaurus source
# content with frontmatter). Ignoring the glob would silently skip
# any NEW authored content for new packages (e.g. someone authoring
# `docs/content/payments.md`). The discriminator between authored
# and generator-output `.md` here is "has Docusaurus frontmatter" —
# not expressible in gitignore. Better to let the trap re-bite a
# careful committer than to silently hide legitimate authoring.
docs/docs/build-*
